/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Take the surroundings as a large reservoir at temperature T₀.
   - For a steady-flow unit with negligible kinetic and potential energy changes, take work input as positive and write Wideal = ΔH − T₀ΔS.
   - The same ideas are also called exergy or availability analysis.
   - Wideal is reversible work input in kJ (negative means work output); ΔH is outlet minus inlet enthalpy in kJ; ΔS is outlet minus inlet entropy in kJ/K; T₀ is dead-state temperature in K.
   - The second law gives the price of irreversibility.
   - Lost work is also called exergy destruction.
   - Use T₀, not the hot or cold stream temperature, because the environment is the only free heat reservoir.
   - Wlost is lost work in kJ; T₀ is dead-state temperature in K; Sgen is total entropy generation in kJ/K.
*/
