/* book Worked example: Q: An ideal Rankine cycle has steam at 4 MPa and 400 °C entering the turbine and a condenser at 10 kPa. Steam-table values: at 4 MPa, 400 °C, h₃ = 3214.4 kJ/kg and s₃ = 6.7712 kJ/(kg·K); at 10 kPa, hf = 191.8 kJ/kg, hfg = 2392.1 kJ/kg, sf = 0.6492 kJ/(kg·K), sfg = 7.4997 kJ/(kg·K), vf = 0.001010 m³/kg. Find the pump work, turbine work, heat added, efficiency and heat rejected. Then find the efficiency if the turbine is 85 % efficient.
   1. State 1 (saturated liquid at 10 kPa): h₁ = 191.8 kJ/kg. Pump: wp = vf(pb − pc) = 0.001010 × (4000 − 10) = 4.03 kJ/kg, so h₂ = 191.8 + 4.0 = 195.8 kJ/kg.
   2. Turbine exit, isentropic: s₄ = s₃ = 6.7712, so x₄ = (6.7712 − 0.6492)/7.4997 = 0.8163 and h₄ = 191.8 + 0.8163 × 2392.1 = 2144.5 kJ/kg.
   3. wt = h₃ − h₄ = 3214.4 − 2144.5 = 1069.9 kJ/kg; wnet = 1069.9 − 4.0 = 1065.9 kJ/kg.
   4. qin = h₃ − h₂ = 3214.4 − 195.8 = 3018.6 kJ/kg; η = 1065.9/3018.6 = 0.353, that is 35.3 percent.
   5. qout = h₄ − h₁ = 2144.5 − 191.8 = 1952.7 kJ/kg. Check: qin − qout = 1065.9 kJ/kg = wnet.
   6. With ηt = 0.85: wt = 0.85 × 1069.9 = 909.4 kJ/kg, h₄ = 3214.4 − 909.4 = 2305.0 kJ/kg (x₄ = 0.883), and η = (909.4 − 4.0)/3018.6 = 0.300.
   Answer: wp = 4.0 kJ/kg, wt = 1069.9 kJ/kg, qin = 3018.6 kJ/kg, η = 35.3 % and qout = 1952.7 kJ/kg; with an 85 % turbine η falls to 30.0 %. */
