/* book exam traps: Using turbine work alone as net work. Subtract the pump work: wnet = wt − wp. | Taking qin from the condenser exit enthalpy h₁. The boiler receives feedwater after the pump, so use h₂ = h₁ + wp. | Mixing bar, kPa and MPa in wp = vf Δp. Convert pressure difference to kPa so that vf in m³/kg gives kJ/kg directly. | Confusing turbine isentropic efficiency (actual against ideal expansion) with cycle efficiency (net work against boiler heat). | Saying the condenser temperature stays constant throughout. It stays at Tsat only while the steam is wet; if the condensate is subcooled, the last part of the condenser cools liquid below saturation. */
